text:
anika: Quick check — third-party backup vendor (BackSafe) needs to push backups from our staging cluster to their S3 in partner account. They want outbound to s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:443. Do we approve NAT egress for the staging subnet or prefer a VPC endpoint + cross-account role? Also: what logs/manifest fields must be redacted for PII before we ship?

kevin: Recommend avoiding opening NAT. Prefer a gateway VPC endpoint for S3 + bucket policy scoped to SourceVpc/SourceAccount. Keeps traffic off the public internet. :+1:

maria: Agreed. Use gateway VPCE for S3. Add bucket policy with Condition on aws:SourceVpcArn and Principal restricted to the vendor role ARN. Also we should strip user emails from object metadata — that’s PII.

anika: Thanks. One more on manifests: our backup manifest currently includes `owner_email` and `initiator_id`. Is it ok to redact `owner_email` and replace with an internal uid? Who signs off for that change?

jason: Security stance: redact emails before export. Replace with internal_id. Keep `initiator_id` for audit (can be pseudonymized if needed). If any user-identifying data leaves our account, get DPO approval.

sec-bot: Policy check: exports of user PII to third parties require DPO approval per Data Export Policy v2.0 — https://redwood/internal/policy/data-export. This thread has been flagged for review.

anika: Ack. Filing DPO ticket now. Also sharing a sample bucket policy I plan to put in the PR: 

```json
{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement":[
    {
      "Effect":"Allow",
      "Principal":{"AWS":"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/backsafe-role"},
      "Action":["s3:PutObject","s3:PutObjectAcl"],
      "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::redwood-staging-backups/*",
      "Condition":{
        "StringEquals":{
          "aws:SourceVpc":"vpc-0abc1234"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

kevin: Policy looks good. Ops note: do NOT enable 0.0.0.0/0 outbound on staging NAT. If vendor absolutely needs outbound to fetch callbacks, we can allow a short-lived, timeboxed rule and document justification in the PR.

maria: :thumbsup: I’ll prep the infra PR with the bucket policy + VPCE route table change and attach the DPO ticket number.

anika: Thanks all. Leaving this thread blocking until DPO signoff. Ping me if you need ARNs or the manifest scrubber script.

jason: If DPO denies, fallback plan is to pull backups into our internal ingestion endpoint that strips PII before forwarding to vendor.

kevin: :eyes:
